{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army","id":1068358,"title":"[2E] How to run the army?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-26T11:35:01-07:00","id":1068358,"title":"[2E] How to run the army?","content":"In my British <b>Mage</b> chronicle players will be in 15 minutes attacked by the two chopper of military soldiers under commands from local Knights of Saint George. I just wonder if there are good military tactics on wizards? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or at least if there is better way to run two choppers with 10 infantry soldiers each on it in combat scenes? Or should I just makes normal mortal PC stats of one soldier NPC and use it 20 times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T17:18:28-07:00","id":1068485,"title":"","content":"Well if it's an urban environment they would repel down from the helicopters under the cover of smoke grenades and then the birds would stay in the area to provide &quot;eyes in the sky&quot; or fire support if you wanna be that hard on the players.<br /> <br /> As for stats I would just use the npc Soldier stats 20 times unless you want to embed a &quot;special forces&quot; a.k.a full hunter in the mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T23:38:47-07:00","id":1068562,"title":"","content":"It's open terrain, hill in deep Britain, but only 15 miles from nearest military base. So 'full desant' should be in order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T15:31:32-07:00","id":1068903,"title":"","content":"What are their orders and mission?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T16:47:38-07:00","id":1068934,"title":"","content":"Helicopters are horrible vehicles to attack mages in, as it takes very little magic to render them inoperable, sending them crashing, causing them to explode, and in doing so killing everyone on board.<br /> <br /> Plus since they're loud you'd be able to target them via Sensory Range very easily.<br /> <br /> I believe attack helicopters are in one of the Armory books, yes, Armory with specific guns at around page 110. If you want people shooting out from them you could use a Teamwork roll, with their firing adding to the helicopter's dicepool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-27-2017, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T18:26:49-07:00","id":1068967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1068903#post1068903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are their orders and mission?</div> </div> </div> </div>Search and destroy witches!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1068934#post1068934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Helicopters are horrible vehicles to attack mages in, as it takes very little magic to render them inoperable, sending them crashing, causing them to explode, and in doing so killing everyone on board.<br /> <br /> Plus since they're loud you'd be able to target them via Sensory Range very easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot get them by submarine on the Hill, can I? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe better would be Armored Car?<br /> <br /> Still, my main thing is - Let PC cast all their spells wants. We talk here about circa 30 Sleepers. It's at least 9-Again on the automatic Paradox rolls... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Even 'system malfuncion' spells can be said to generate them with simple 'we make sure all our machines are good - and we hunt witches!'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1068934#post1068934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe attack helicopters are in one of the Armory books, yes, Armory with specific guns at around page 110. If you want people shooting out from them you could use a Teamwork roll, with their firing adding to the helicopter's dicepool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, will check it now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T18:55:48-07:00","id":1068974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1068967#post1068967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot get them by submarine on the Hill, can I? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe better would be Armored Car?<br /> <br /> Still, my main thing is - Let PC cast all their spells wants. We talk here about circa 30 Sleepers. It's at least 9-Again on the automatic Paradox rolls... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Even 'system malfuncion' spells can be said to generate them with simple 'we make sure all our machines are good - and we hunt witches!'</div> </div> </div> </div>Ballistic missiles from a submarine can fire well onto the mainland and would cause Aggravated damage. A battleship could do something similar. Though I think, no guarantee, that would be harder to organize than a helicopter strike.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, a better bet would just be a group of soldiers who can hit a target reliably at medium-to-long range. Not necessarily snipers, just firing at a decent distance such that they would be hard to pin them down with magic in return. Don't have them massed up, either, so they couldn't all be targeted with a single spell. Your other group would be closer up, throwing some tear gas and stun grenades which would disable the mages, making it much harder for them to really do anything but be mowed down or flee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-27-2017, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T19:14:47-07:00","id":1068980,"title":"","content":"Problem is that PC mages took hostage local military commander / high Knights of Saint George agent. Killing witches is a means to recover the target commander, not by destroying everything on their way, as they can kill commander also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T19:15:41-07:00","id":1068981,"title":"","content":"Depending on visibility and weather conditions it's very hard to spot a helicopter at night, and while they are pretty loud when they are on top of you not so much a mile out. More then likely they would drop the troops a ways out and then perform close air support once the troops engage the mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T00:31:41-07:00","id":1069179,"title":"","content":"How powerful are the mages in question and are they ready for retaliation? Also, does the army in question have any ways of piercing magical defenses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T00:47:58-07:00","id":1069186,"title":"","content":"Gnosis circa 6, Arcana 4-5. Army can have any defense a Knight of Saint George can provide. Plus few of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/499949-art-of-witch-hunting-htv-perspective?p=508782#post508782\">my own fan ideas</a> - like 'Mage Armor pricing bullets'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T01:34:02-07:00","id":1069200,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I don't really know what the Knights of Saint George can do, but assuming your mage players decide to ward the place they're in against detection or cut off access, do they have a reliable way of bypassing that? Assuming they have access to pretty much every arcana at 4 they could pretty easily do things like putting a giant ban or incognito presence on the area in which they're holding their captive. That's something you're really going to need to take into consideration.<br /> <br /> Also, do they have anything to stop them from just teleporting away or hiding in the Shadow or Death/Spirit/or even Mind attuned Twilight? Thinking about it, since we're talking Masters here, they could just create gates to the Underworld or even the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-28-2017, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T13:13:54-07:00","id":1069569,"title":"","content":"The Soldiers can be sleepers but they'll need at least a couple Sleepwalker Knights with them. I came up with &quot;Eldritch Rounds&quot; for For my Task Force: Valkyrie game that did aggravated damage to mages and imposed a penalty on dice pools for spellcasting up to -5 from being shot. The idea was that an anonymous benefactor showed TFV enigmatic runes that messed with mages and their ability to do magic (abyssal runes most likely) and that is was entirely likely that R&amp;D would find a way to adapt those runes to making wards and barriers that resisted magic or nullified it. I don't know much about the KoSG abilities, but they could do something with that. Basically if you can keep a Mage from casting then they're pretty easy to take out, that's why you bring sleepers to cause Paradox. Helicopters are probably a poor choice for taking on mages, you want to catch a Mage off guard with sudden surgical strikes. Generally taking on a Mage cabal is a months long process of collecting information, mapping out their routines and identifying family, friends and loved ones. I might suggest using the KoSG more heavily as the actual combatants and the soldiers are just to cause a distraction and cause Paradox.<br /> <br /> On actually building the soldiers, I'd just make maybe two or three and just duplicate them. I would add a complete team of Knights though, if you want to be really mean you can give them conviction and skill tricks from Mirrors. The mages could still probably teleport away but that just means they are on the run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T23:50:39-07:00","id":1069914,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it - 'corruption' of choppers engines, leading to it's crash, can be easily solution to sorceres problems. But then they will kill 20-30 people in one action - so almost surely will hit their Wisdom scores. Even this scenario I like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069200#post1069200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, I don't really know what the Knights of Saint George can do, but assuming your mage players decide to ward the place they're in against detection or cut off access, do they have a reliable way of bypassing that? Assuming they have access to pretty much every arcana at 4 they could pretty easily do things like putting a giant ban or incognito presence on the area in which they're holding their captive. That's something you're really going to need to take into consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knights with soldiers ( first group, now hostages ) were send to precise location my mages looks for. Military have direct location coordinates. PCs can make hostages, for example, invisible, but it will only makes matter worse - as 'choppers group' ( second one ) will not see people they were looking for, but only six witches I assume they will kill to 'monsters' first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069200#post1069200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, do they have anything to stop them from just teleporting away or hiding in the Shadow or Death/Spirit/or even Mind attuned Twilight? Thinking about it, since we're talking Masters here, they could just create gates to the Underworld or even the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing. But each spell in eyes of Sleepers... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T23:58:46-07:00","id":1069915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069569#post1069569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Soldiers can be sleepers but they'll need at least a couple Sleepwalker Knights with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>My standard Witch Hunting 'tactics' - make Conspiracy agents with Endowments ( i.e. Sleepwalkers ) commanders of unit to use their supernatural powers. And all the rest are Sleepers to make Paradox rolls for mages and aggrevate them to 9 or 8 Again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069569#post1069569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I came up with &quot;Eldritch Rounds&quot; for For my Task Force: Valkyrie game that did aggravated damage to mages and imposed a penalty on dice pools for spellcasting up to -5 from being shot. The idea was that an anonymous benefactor showed TFV enigmatic runes that messed with mages and their ability to do magic (abyssal runes most likely) and that is was entirely likely that R&amp;D would find a way to adapt those runes to making wards and barriers that resisted magic or nullified it. I don't know much about the KoSG abilities, but they could do something with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Intrigiuing, will think about using those, thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069569#post1069569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically if you can keep a Mage from casting then they're pretty easy to take out, that's why you bring sleepers to cause Paradox. Helicopters are probably a poor choice for taking on mages, you want to catch a Mage off guard with sudden surgical strikes. Generally taking on a Mage cabal is a months long process of collecting information, mapping out their routines and identifying family, friends and loved ones. I might suggest using the KoSG more heavily as the actual combatants and the soldiers are just to cause a distraction and cause Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>PCs just take most of KoSG agents in region - 2-3 of rest will be on Helicopters. More of them would be too much a streach in 'middle of nowhere' in Britain. As to Helicopters - I written already. If players will take Helicopters full of people before combat, it will be killing 30 people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069569#post1069569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mages could still probably teleport away but that just means they are on the run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's mages problem if they want to run from the place - it's wizards who want to explore this place. Knights can easily just sit there and wait for them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T00:12:49-07:00","id":1069918,"title":"","content":"Thinking about running army as Violence Group from <b>Hurt Locker </b>- but then, stats of Violence Groups are too low for professional military units, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-29-2017, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T01:33:31-07:00","id":1069925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069914#post1069914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knights with soldiers ( first group, now hostages ) were send to precise location my mages looks for. Military have direct location coordinates. PCs can make hostages, for example, invisible, but it will only makes matter worse - as 'choppers group' ( second one ) will not see people they were looking for, but only six witches I assume they will kill to 'monsters' first.<br /> <br /> Nothing. But each spell in eyes of Sleepers... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, what I mean is, do they have any way to counter not being able to perceive <i>anyone</i> there, the mages included? Just using an example, but Incognito Presence can hide everything in the area from mundane perception in a way similar to Obfuscate. Even if they know their exact coordinates they still won't be able to actually notice them. So they could make the hostage, themselves, and even the place they're holed up in completely undetectable using mundane means. Do the Knights of Saint George you're sending against them have a way to bypass something like that?<br /> <br /> And each spell can be in the eyes of a Sleeper but does it really matter when all it takes is one? Sure, that one will add +1 Paradox die and maybe even Rote Action on the Paradox dice pool assuming there are enough Sleepers there directly witnessing them cast it, but that isn't <i>that</i> bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-29-2017, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T01:50:16-07:00","id":1069930,"title":"","content":"So when you say they are a few miles from the base do you mean inside the base parameter or outside over looking the base?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T02:08:06-07:00","id":1069935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069925#post1069925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, what I mean is, do they have any way to counter not being able to perceive <i>anyone</i> there, the mages included? Just using an example, but Incognito Presence can hide everything in the area from mundane perception in a way similar to Obfuscate. Even if they know their exact coordinates they still won't be able to actually notice them. So they could make the hostage, themselves, and even the place they're holed up in completely undetectable using mundane means. Do the Knights of Saint George you're sending against them have a way to bypass something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basiclly, cause Knights know they are after witches ( from communicate first group send before capturing ) they have SOME ways to prepare themselves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>Incognito Presence</i> <i>do not</i> make you invisible - it makes you <u>unnoticeable</u>. You still are registered, you just look like 'that guy in the street'. And what look like witches does not important. See probable dialog:<br /> '&lt;From chopper&gt; Sir, we are on location of call for backup. On hill there are only six... nobodies. Some sort of bumms.<br /> &lt;Answer of commander&gt; Shoot on sight! They must be witches!'<br /> <br /> <i>Invisibility </i>spell, from Forces, would make you classically Predator-style invisible. But then, on infrared radiation you still will be seen - and Infrared Googles are on standard NATO equipment.<br /> <br /> And to Knights of Saint George - they easily can have Endowment - probably small Goetic Demon - that goes to after nearest stores of Mana. And mages are living stores of Mana... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T03:01:42-07:00","id":1069946,"title":"","content":"Without looking at the book it would be just an extra Reach to cover more than the visible spectrum. But that's if your players think that far ahead. You don't necessarily need to notify them of that option.<br /> <br /> However, there are still three types of Twilight, and humans have a bit of trouble interacting with beings in Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T03:06:43-07:00","id":1069949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069946#post1069946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, there are still three types of Twilight, and humans have a bit of trouble interacting with beings in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, mages will jump into Twilight. Now they won't go to the Astral Realm Iris they want to be in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They <i>must</i> be in Material world to use Astral mind-portal they are after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T03:46:50-07:00","id":1069954,"title":"","content":"Is that something specific to that particular iris or a house rule? By the book Twilight is still part of the material. It is, by definition, the state of existence for ephemeral entities when they are in the material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T03:49:24-07:00","id":1069955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069954#post1069954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that something specific to that particular iris or a house rule? By the book Twilight is still part of the material. It is, by definition, the state of existence for ephemeral entities when they are in the material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I do not know on this. It was my interpretation from rules that you cannot 'touch' Iris in Twillight. But it's somehow niche example that should be answered, in seperate topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T03:59:41-07:00","id":1069959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069935#post1069935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Incognito Presence</i> <i>do not</i> make you invisible - it makes you <u>unnoticeable</u>. You still are registered, you just look like 'that guy in the street'. And what look like witches does not important. See probable dialog:<br /> '&lt;From chopper&gt; Sir, we are on location of call for backup. On hill there are only six... nobodies. Some sort of bumms.<br /> &lt;Answer of commander&gt; Shoot on sight! They must be witches!'</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, that's not how Incognito works in 2e. The spell immediately wipes them from memory after you look away, and it also forces a clash of wills to make the person to look away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And to Knights of Saint George - they easily can have Endowment - probably small Goetic Demon - that goes to after nearest stores of Mana. And mages are living stores of Mana... </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd build at least some of the Knights as Banishers; I mean, yeah that's not precisely right, but the Knights are very close to being low powered banishers anyway. Just say the Goetic Gospels give them access to magic rather than the standard endowments. Giving them the ability to use magic would allow them to level the playing field a lot.<br /> <br /> Honestly, from what you've said about this group before, it sounds like they're going to nuke those helicopters the moment they appear and just take the wisdom hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T04:46:39-07:00","id":1069972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069959#post1069959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, that's not how Incognito works in 2e. The spell immediately wipes them from memory after you look away, and it also forces a clash of wills to make the person to look away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dammit! Too easy then. Oh, well, some Endowment to 'check active spells' will be enough to bypass it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069959#post1069959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd build at least some of the Knights as Banishers; I mean, yeah that's not precisely right, but the Knights are very close to being low powered banishers anyway. Just say the Goetic Gospels give them access to magic rather than the standard endowments. Giving them the ability to use magic would allow them to level the playing field a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno - would not Banishers in ranks of Sleepers lead to VERY unstable mob of Sleepers? Banishers spells lead to falling Integrity just the same as normal mages...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069959#post1069959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, from what you've said about this group before, it sounds like they're going to nuke those helicopters the moment they appear and just take the wisdom hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no problem with that - if their conscience and Wisdom handel this... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I mean, they are Double Adepts and Masters - there are not really many things that can stop them. So it's damn time they Wisdom will slip more and more and we see how future Messiahs of Magic become 'monsters' witches are assumed to be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-29-2017, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T05:14:52-07:00","id":1069988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1069972#post1069972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dammit! Too easy then. Oh, well, some Endowment to 'check active spells' will be enough to bypass it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably want something a bit more pro-active like an active cancelation endowment. Just knowing there's an active spell around isn't going to help that much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dunno - would not Banishers in ranks of Sleepers lead to VERY unstable mob of Sleepers? Banishers spells lead to falling Integrity just the same as normal mages... </div> </div> </div>Depends what they're doing. There are a lot of subtle things they can do to even the playing field. Also, these are KoSG agents, they're probably already pretty unstable to begin with.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you don't have to have them be Banishers exactly. You could just use the magic system to simulate a more flexible Goetic Gospels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have no problem with that - if their conscience and Wisdom handel this... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I mean, they are Double Adepts and Masters - there are not really many things that can stop them. So it's damn time they Wisdom will slip more and more and we see how future Messiahs of Magic become 'monsters' witches are assumed to be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>You know your group best. They have already taken a hostage, they don't sound terribly nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T06:33:53-07:00","id":1070016,"title":"","content":"The clear sighted merit from vampire 2e gives a human the ability to see past past obfuscate and says &quot;other similar abilities&quot;. Could houserule it as being able to see past incognito since it works similarly to obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T07:23:55-07:00","id":1070044,"title":"","content":"For taking down some of the harder magical protections, you could (as mentioned) toss in a &quot;repentant&quot; Banisher among the KoSG ranks as a specialist (or even a Proximus, Relic Attuned, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=953939#post953939\">Spell-Thief</a>, or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068636-the-soul-shaped\">Soul-Shaped</a> of some counter-magic Legacy).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T09:43:52-07:00","id":1070162,"title":"","content":"It's as Michael says, you're going to need something to actually cancel effects. The Incognito Presence example was just a soft check, you're going to also need to be able to get around effects like Ban. At that point, even knowing exactly where they are and seeing the active magic isn't going to do anything for them since they simply have no way of bypassing warped space. Anything they try to shoot in will just come out the other side, and you can't interact with it directly any better than you could normal space since it isn't like it's a solid physical barrier.<br /> <br /> And while Dissonance might eventually get through you don't even start rolling for its effects until the <i>end</i> of the scene in which they encounter the active magic, and by then it's probably going to be too late. So they're likely going to need a Merit/Endowment to even detect that there is a spell hiding shit from them and then <i>another</i> Endowment to cancel said active spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T10:06:34-07:00","id":1070175,"title":"","content":"Looking over it again, the Goetic Gospels look much better than I remember. The Lie of the Heart from the Gospel of Agares would seem to combat Incognito Prescence pretty well, though the rules are a little odd. The Knight has to roll over the dot rating of the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T10:20:10-07:00","id":1070181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1070175#post1070175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking over it again, the Goetic Gospels look much better than I remember. The Lie of the Heart from the Gospel of Agares would seem to combat Incognito Prescence pretty well, though the rules are a little odd. The Knight has to roll over the dot rating of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's first edition, it might take a bit of alteration to make it work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T10:54:59-07:00","id":1070199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1070181#post1070181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's first edition, it might take a bit of alteration to make it work.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would still be odd in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T11:36:45-07:00","id":1070213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1070199#post1070199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would still be odd in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>As in the Spell dots or having to roll above it in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T13:38:03-07:00","id":1070270,"title":"","content":"The spell dots. Like, it doesn't take into account the power of the mage. An ascended archmaster is treated the same as an Apprentice.<br /> <br /> I dunno, maybe that's common and I've just never come across it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T14:12:30-07:00","id":1070291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1068358-2e-how-to-run-the-army?p=1070270#post1070270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell dots. Like, it doesn't take into account the power of the mage. An ascended archmaster is treated the same as an Apprentice.<br /> <br /> I dunno, maybe that's common and I've just never come across it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Goetic Gospels are likely coming from Abyssal Entities. We know how those guys make magic go haywire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","ti